  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating differences between outcomes and a reference value (set at -500 for Lottery A), computing the weighted mean of these differences, and preferring the lottery with the more favorable (i.e., higher) mean difference. In this case, both lotteries have a mean difference of zero. The individual, however, does not mention the reference value, nor does the individual compute or refer to differences from it. Instead, the individual's justification is based solely on the probability of losing (50% vs. 100%), which reflects a different reasoning process — one focused on risk exposure rather than mean differences from a reference. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason's rule. The reasoning described is inconsistent with the required components of the decision reason (reference value, differences, weighted mean differences).",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

